1
00:00:00,120 --> 00:00:04,440
Imagine waking up before dawn, not for work, not for a trip, nor even to hit the gym.

2
00:00:04,440 --> 00:00:08,680
You wake up because the street is starting to wake up, and you need to find a safe place before the rush begins.

3
00:00:08,680 --> 00:00:11,560
Now imagine the same morning, but in a small house.

4
00:00:11,560 --> 00:00:17,640
And then a few levels up, a comfortable house, then a villa, and then a house where you have a full team managing the details of your day.

5
00:00:17,640 --> 00:00:23,860
The same day, the same 24 hours, but every financial level changes how you use your time, money, and health.

6
00:00:23,860 --> 00:00:26,340
And even the number of problems you need to think about yourself.

7
00:00:26,500 --> 00:00:31,300
Today we will live a full day, from the person who has no shelter to the person who owns a fortune in the billions.

8
00:00:31,300 --> 00:00:36,820
And the real question isn't who has more money. The question is how life itself changes when the financial level changes.

9
00:00:36,820 --> 00:00:42,490
Without shelter: You wake up before dawn because the street gets noisy as the city starts moving.

10
00:00:42,490 --> 00:00:48,090
Your body is aching and stiff from sleeping on concrete, a park bench, or a mattress in a shelter.

11
00:00:48,090 --> 00:00:53,720
The first thing you do is check your few belongings and make sure nothing was stolen from you in the night.

12
00:00:53,900 --> 00:00:56,300
If you have a phone, it's usually old.

13
00:00:56,300 --> 00:00:58,700
The screen is cracked, and the battery dies quickly.

14
00:00:58,700 --> 00:01:03,660
So you look for free Wi-Fi as if you're looking for treasure, and charging is another problem in itself.

15
00:01:03,660 --> 00:01:06,300
After that, the first goal is a bathroom and water.

16
00:01:06,300 --> 00:01:11,580
You go to a restaurant, a gas station, a library, or a public park, hoping the staff won't kick you out.

17
00:01:11,580 --> 00:01:15,180
If you find a place where you can use the bathroom, you go in quickly.

18
00:01:15,180 --> 00:01:19,700
You wash your face and body in the simplest way possible and try to groom yourself.

19
00:01:19,780 --> 00:01:21,780
Clean clothes here aren't a normal thing.

20
00:01:21,780 --> 00:01:24,460
Clean clothes are a rare currency.

21
00:01:24,460 --> 00:01:28,700
Then comes food; you look for a free breakfast at a charity.

22
00:01:28,700 --> 00:01:32,380
Or the cheapest meal you can buy with the few dollars you have.

23
00:01:32,380 --> 00:01:35,660
And if you have a food stamp card, you buy simple groceries.

24
00:01:35,660 --> 00:01:37,020
But you have a problem.

25
00:01:37,020 --> 00:01:38,470
You don't own a kitchen.

26
00:01:38,470 --> 00:01:40,710
So you eat what you can carry with you.

27
00:01:40,710 --> 00:01:43,020
Hunger is always close by.

28
00:01:43,020 --> 00:01:45,660
Even your plan for the day isn't built on rest.

29
00:01:45,660 --> 00:01:49,660
It's built on safety, the weather, and places you can sit in.

30
00:01:49,660 --> 00:01:51,110
Without anyone kicking you out.

31
00:01:51,110 --> 00:01:52,550
The public library, for you, is...

32
00:01:52,550 --> 00:01:53,270
A treasure.

33
00:01:53,270 --> 00:01:54,070
A chair.

34
00:01:54,070 --> 00:01:54,950
Wi-Fi.

35
00:01:54,950 --> 00:01:55,830
A power outlet.

36
00:01:55,830 --> 00:01:57,930
And a place where you can look for work.

37
00:01:57,930 --> 00:01:59,210
Even if you're begging.

38
00:01:59,210 --> 00:02:01,290
You pick a corner with foot traffic.

39
00:02:01,290 --> 00:02:02,970
But far from trouble.

40
00:02:02,970 --> 00:02:05,050
The little money accumulates slowly.

41
00:02:05,050 --> 00:02:06,730
And sometimes a whole day passes.

42
00:02:06,730 --> 00:02:08,300
And you get nothing at all.

43
00:02:08,300 --> 00:02:09,820
Then comes the biggest problem.

44
00:02:09,820 --> 00:02:11,270
Official papers.

45
00:02:11,270 --> 00:02:12,310
You don't have an ID.

46
00:02:12,310 --> 00:02:15,110
Accessing a job, housing, or aid becomes...

47
00:02:15,110 --> 00:02:16,230
Much harder.

48
00:02:16,230 --> 00:02:17,310
You want to get an ID?

49
00:02:17,390 --> 00:02:18,190
You need time.

50
00:02:18,190 --> 00:02:18,830
And fees.

51
00:02:18,830 --> 00:02:19,710
And procedures.

52
00:02:19,710 --> 00:02:20,950
And sometimes an address.

53
00:02:20,950 --> 00:02:22,670
And you don't even have an address.

54
00:02:22,670 --> 00:02:24,370
Health is another issue entirely.

55
00:02:24,370 --> 00:02:26,730
A visit to the ER might be your only solution.

56
00:02:26,730 --> 00:02:28,690
Or you wait at a free clinic for hours.

57
00:02:28,690 --> 00:02:30,250
Even medications, you need to store them.

58
00:02:30,250 --> 00:02:31,690
And sleep itself is hard to secure.

59
00:02:31,690 --> 00:02:33,610
And at night, the same cycle begins.

60
00:02:33,610 --> 00:02:34,730
Where to sleep?

61
00:02:34,730 --> 00:02:36,730
Shelters have rules and lines.

62
00:02:36,730 --> 00:02:38,670
And the street is noisy and dangerous.

63
00:02:38,670 --> 00:02:40,910
You hide your valuables inside your clothes.

64
00:02:40,910 --> 00:02:42,550
And you sleep lightly.

65
00:02:42,550 --> 00:02:43,480
And tomorrow.

66
00:02:43,480 --> 00:02:44,680
Morning comes early.

67
00:02:44,680 --> 00:02:46,200
And you repeat the same routine.

68
00:02:46,200 --> 00:02:46,840
Water.

69
00:02:46,840 --> 00:02:47,400
Food.

70
00:02:47,400 --> 00:02:47,840
Safety.

71
00:02:47,840 --> 00:02:50,830
And a plan to survive just one more day.

72
00:02:50,830 --> 00:02:52,400
The Second Class.

73
00:02:52,400 --> 00:02:55,290
Extreme Poverty.

74
00:02:55,290 --> 00:02:56,650
Here, you have a roof.

75
00:02:56,650 --> 00:02:59,170
But it barely counts as safety.

76
00:02:59,170 --> 00:03:00,890
You might wake up in a small room.

77
00:03:00,890 --> 00:03:02,490
Rented by the week.

78
00:03:02,490 --> 00:03:03,890
Or a crowded apartment you share.

79
00:03:03,890 --> 00:03:05,010
With more than one person.

80
00:03:05,010 --> 00:03:06,710
To split the rent.

81
00:03:06,710 --> 00:03:08,310
A mattress on the floor, and sometimes the AC.

82
00:03:08,310 --> 00:03:09,470
Or the heater is broken.

83
00:03:09,470 --> 00:03:11,270
First, you check your prepaid phone.

84
00:03:11,270 --> 00:03:12,510
Is the service still active?

85
00:03:12,590 --> 00:03:14,830
Then you remember the transit pass left in your wallet.

86
00:03:14,830 --> 00:03:16,590
And you start planning your day around money.

87
00:03:16,590 --> 00:03:17,470
Breakfast is basic.

88
00:03:17,470 --> 00:03:18,030
Oats.

89
00:03:18,030 --> 00:03:18,430
Eggs.

90
00:03:18,430 --> 00:03:18,750
Toast.

91
00:03:18,750 --> 00:03:19,670
Simple groceries.

92
00:03:19,670 --> 00:03:20,590
You use coupons.

93
00:03:20,590 --> 00:03:21,470
And food stamps.

94
00:03:21,470 --> 00:03:22,910
And charity schedules.

95
00:03:22,910 --> 00:03:23,870
Everything is calculated.

96
00:03:23,870 --> 00:03:25,250
And if you have kids.

97
00:03:25,250 --> 00:03:27,450
A part of their diet might rely on school meals.

98
00:03:27,450 --> 00:03:28,890
And you prepare a snack for them from home.

99
00:03:28,890 --> 00:03:30,170
Because every riyal makes a difference.

100
00:03:30,170 --> 00:03:31,570
The commute to work takes time.

101
00:03:31,570 --> 00:03:33,380
You wait for a bus that's late.

102
00:03:33,380 --> 00:03:34,620
Or you drive a beat-up car.

103
00:03:34,620 --> 00:03:35,780
With the check engine light on.

104
00:03:35,780 --> 00:03:37,420
And you say, "I'll fix it later."

105
00:03:37,420 --> 00:03:38,620
Your work hours might change.

106
00:03:38,620 --> 00:03:40,020
Every week, one day they call you in.

107
00:03:40,020 --> 00:03:41,510
And another day they don't.

108
00:03:41,510 --> 00:03:43,110
That's why you say yes to any extra shift.

109
00:03:43,110 --> 00:03:44,350
Or a day job you can manage.

110
00:03:44,350 --> 00:03:45,870
You can't risk saying no.

111
00:03:45,870 --> 00:03:47,150
Tips and overtime.

112
00:03:47,150 --> 00:03:48,270
Here, they aren't a luxury.

113
00:03:48,270 --> 00:03:50,460
Sometimes they are what keeps the electricity on.

114
00:03:50,460 --> 00:03:51,260
The bills themselves.

115
00:03:51,260 --> 00:03:52,580
Have become a puzzle to solve every month.

116
00:03:52,580 --> 00:03:53,100
Rent is due.

117
00:03:53,100 --> 00:03:54,220
The electric bill is past due.

118
00:03:54,220 --> 00:03:55,620
And the other bill is waiting.

119
00:03:55,620 --> 00:03:57,140
You choose which late fee is less painful.

120
00:03:57,140 --> 00:03:59,180
The way you pay is something you think about.

121
00:03:59,180 --> 00:04:00,140
You buy a money order.

122
00:04:00,140 --> 00:04:01,820
Because you're avoiding bank fees.

123
00:04:01,820 --> 00:04:03,710
And the paperwork never ends. Health.

124
00:04:03,710 --> 00:04:05,150
A clinic appointment is weeks away.

125
00:04:05,150 --> 00:04:07,700
Or the ER when the pain gets stronger than the wait.

126
00:04:07,700 --> 00:04:09,980
And insurance, if it exists...

127
00:04:09,980 --> 00:04:12,060
Might be limited or have a high deductible.

128
00:04:12,060 --> 00:04:13,780
Even fixing your teeth gets postponed.

129
00:04:13,780 --> 00:04:15,140
Because you have more important things.

130
00:04:15,140 --> 00:04:16,700
Laundry takes money and time.

131
00:04:16,700 --> 00:04:18,540
So you combine it with the laundromat trip.

132
00:04:18,540 --> 00:04:20,140
And take advantage of the free Wi-Fi.

133
00:04:20,140 --> 00:04:21,180
To look for jobs.

134
00:04:21,180 --> 00:04:22,100
And learn from YouTube.

135
00:04:22,100 --> 00:04:24,340
How to fix your things with tape and glue.

136
00:04:24,340 --> 00:04:26,620
Here, everything has a longer lifespan than it should.

137
00:04:26,620 --> 00:04:28,900
Soap, gas, mobile data.

138
00:04:29,300 --> 00:04:30,100
Even patience.

139
00:04:30,100 --> 00:04:31,580
And at night, you prepare for tomorrow's schedule.

140
00:04:31,580 --> 00:04:33,820
You set two alarms and make a simple list.

141
00:04:33,820 --> 00:04:34,460
A call.

142
00:04:34,460 --> 00:04:35,020
An appointment.

143
00:04:35,020 --> 00:04:35,620
Charity.

144
00:04:35,620 --> 00:04:36,100
Work.

145
00:04:36,100 --> 00:04:37,020
And then you sleep.

146
00:04:37,020 --> 00:04:39,560
Because tomorrow you have the same race.

147
00:04:39,560 --> 00:04:41,200
The Third Class.

148
00:04:41,200 --> 00:04:42,600
The Working Poor.

149
00:04:42,600 --> 00:04:45,640
Here you have a job and an income.

150
00:04:45,720 --> 00:04:48,080
But you are still very close to the edge.

151
00:04:48,080 --> 00:04:50,600
You wake up before the sun to your phone alarm.

152
00:04:50,600 --> 00:04:53,560
You live in a small apartment on a monthly or yearly lease.

153
00:04:53,560 --> 00:04:56,200
And you might share it with roommates to split the cost.

154
00:04:56,200 --> 00:04:57,160
The first thing you do.

155
00:04:57,160 --> 00:04:58,320
You check your banking app.

156
00:04:58,320 --> 00:04:59,640
Did the salary drop yet or not?

157
00:04:59,640 --> 00:05:01,040
You make your coffee at home.

158
00:05:01,040 --> 00:05:02,200
And prepare your lunch.

159
00:05:02,200 --> 00:05:04,480
Because buying food at work strains the budget.

160
00:05:04,480 --> 00:05:06,480
You go to work by bus or an old car.

161
00:05:06,480 --> 00:05:07,920
Gas is calculated to the riyal.

162
00:05:07,920 --> 00:05:09,160
And parking is calculated.

163
00:05:09,200 --> 00:05:11,770
Your job might be in a store or a warehouse.

164
00:05:11,770 --> 00:05:12,890
Or a restaurant, or caregiving.

165
00:05:12,890 --> 00:05:14,450
Standing most of the shift, moving fast.

166
00:05:14,450 --> 00:05:15,690
And following the manager's instructions.

167
00:05:15,690 --> 00:05:17,250
Time is tracked, and breaks are short.

168
00:05:17,250 --> 00:05:19,580
And if there's overtime, you say yes if you can.

169
00:05:19,580 --> 00:05:22,500
Not because you love the extra work, but because you need it.

170
00:05:22,500 --> 00:05:24,460
On your lunch break, you eat what you brought with you.

171
00:05:24,460 --> 00:05:26,060
Then you check the schedule app.

172
00:05:26,060 --> 00:05:27,780
And see next week's shifts.

173
00:05:27,780 --> 00:05:30,570
You try to swap a day if you have a doctor's appointment.

174
00:05:30,570 --> 00:05:32,490
Or a school meeting, or something important for the family.

175
00:05:32,570 --> 00:05:33,770
Health insurance is there.

176
00:05:33,770 --> 00:05:35,170
But the deductible is high.

177
00:05:35,170 --> 00:05:38,170
So you avoid the hospital unless it becomes absolutely necessary.

178
00:05:38,170 --> 00:05:40,490
And you count the hours, because every extra hour...

179
00:05:40,490 --> 00:05:41,730
Can make a difference in the paycheck.

180
00:05:41,730 --> 00:05:44,050
On the way home, you stop at a store with sales.

181
00:05:44,050 --> 00:05:46,090
You use your loyalty card and discount coupons.

182
00:05:46,090 --> 00:05:47,330
You pay today's bill.

183
00:05:47,330 --> 00:05:49,170
And postpone the other one to next week.

184
00:05:49,170 --> 00:05:51,610
And you try to put away even $20 into savings.

185
00:05:51,610 --> 00:05:52,850
Not because the amount is large.

186
00:05:52,850 --> 00:05:54,810
But because you know an emergency fund...

187
00:05:54,810 --> 00:05:56,510
Starts from a small amount.

188
00:05:56,510 --> 00:05:58,590
At home, you do chores, wash clothes.

189
00:05:58,590 --> 00:06:00,510
And hang up your uniform so it's ready.

190
00:06:00,510 --> 00:06:01,310
You open the mail.

191
00:06:01,310 --> 00:06:02,190
A utility bill.

192
00:06:02,190 --> 00:06:03,110
A small credit card balance.

193
00:06:03,110 --> 00:06:04,190
A rent notice.

194
00:06:04,190 --> 00:06:06,710
And amidst this, you send a message about a side gig on the weekend.

195
00:06:06,710 --> 00:06:08,430
You might watch a series on a shared account.

196
00:06:08,430 --> 00:06:11,230
Or you might start an online course for a certificate to help you step up.

197
00:06:11,230 --> 00:06:12,440
And then you sleep.

198
00:06:12,440 --> 00:06:14,970
Six hours if things go well, and tomorrow is the same routine.

199
00:06:14,970 --> 00:06:16,490
The Fourth Class.

200
00:06:16,490 --> 00:06:20,140
The Lower Middle Class.

201
00:06:20,140 --> 00:06:22,950
Here life starts to get a little calmer.

202
00:06:22,950 --> 00:06:25,270
You wake up in a two-bedroom apartment with a living room.

203
00:06:25,270 --> 00:06:26,870
Or a modest small house.

204
00:06:26,870 --> 00:06:29,080
The place is clean and simple.

205
00:06:29,080 --> 00:06:32,310
And on the fridge is a list of bills and their due dates.

206
00:06:32,310 --> 00:06:34,310
The coffee is brewing while you check your calendar.

207
00:06:34,310 --> 00:06:35,790
A stable job with clear hours.

208
00:06:35,790 --> 00:06:37,030
The salary drops every two weeks.

209
00:06:37,030 --> 00:06:39,870
And you have insurance, and a small percentage for retirement is deducted from the salary.

210
00:06:39,870 --> 00:06:41,390
You use a budget app.

211
00:06:41,390 --> 00:06:43,390
And put the basics on auto-deduct.

212
00:06:43,390 --> 00:06:44,430
Breakfast is simple.

213
00:06:45,950 --> 00:06:46,990
And if you have kids.

214
00:06:46,990 --> 00:06:48,990
You prep their lunch and check their homework.

215
00:06:48,990 --> 00:06:50,830
And if you don't, you prep your own lunch.

216
00:06:50,830 --> 00:06:52,470
To save money on the cafeteria at work.

217
00:06:52,470 --> 00:06:54,430
A clean used car that you're paying off in installments.

218
00:06:54,430 --> 00:06:56,030
Or you use a train with a monthly pass.

219
00:06:56,030 --> 00:06:57,630
And gas, insurance, and maintenance.

220
00:06:57,630 --> 00:06:59,790
Are all expenses you anticipate before you pay them.

221
00:06:59,790 --> 00:07:00,950
At work, your role is clear.

222
00:07:00,950 --> 00:07:02,630
You reply to emails, manage orders.

223
00:07:02,630 --> 00:07:04,990
Handle clients or pull reports.

224
00:07:04,990 --> 00:07:06,630
A paid break and lunchtime.

225
00:07:06,630 --> 00:07:09,030
And you generally know your schedule weeks in advance.

226
00:07:09,030 --> 00:07:11,190
You try to save a small portion for retirement.

227
00:07:11,190 --> 00:07:13,670
And you don't touch the emergency fund unless you have to.

228
00:07:13,670 --> 00:07:15,350
At lunch, you open the banking app.

229
00:07:15,350 --> 00:07:17,070
Your student loan installment is withdrawing tomorrow.

230
00:07:17,070 --> 00:07:18,270
So you transfer a little into savings.

231
00:07:18,270 --> 00:07:20,190
And leave a buffer for gas and groceries.

232
00:07:20,190 --> 00:07:22,710
After work, you hit a cheap gym or walk around the neighborhood.

233
00:07:22,710 --> 00:07:24,030
Dinner is mostly home-cooked.

234
00:07:24,030 --> 00:07:25,510
And entertainment is Netflix and the like.

235
00:07:25,510 --> 00:07:27,350
A subscription or two, and you rotate between them.

236
00:07:27,350 --> 00:07:29,430
You plan a short road trip once a year.

237
00:07:29,430 --> 00:07:30,510
And save up for it early on.

238
00:07:40,050 --> 00:07:41,940
The Fifth Class.

239
00:07:41,940 --> 00:07:45,010
The Middle Class.

240
00:07:45,010 --> 00:07:47,770
Here, life begins to enter a phase...

241
00:07:47,770 --> 00:07:49,650
Of true stability.

242
00:07:49,650 --> 00:07:51,570
You wake up in a three-bedroom house.

243
00:07:51,570 --> 00:07:52,970
Or a comfortable apartment.

244
00:07:52,970 --> 00:07:55,560
And you plan to stay there for years.

245
00:07:55,560 --> 00:07:57,800
You have a mortgage or a stable lease.

246
00:07:57,800 --> 00:08:00,040
Heating, AC, and appliances are working.

247
00:08:00,040 --> 00:08:01,480
And the coffee is almost ready.

248
00:08:01,480 --> 00:08:03,280
Like it's part of your official routine.

249
00:08:03,280 --> 00:08:05,440
You check a shared calendar between you and the family.

250
00:08:05,440 --> 00:08:06,740
Salaries are fixed.

251
00:08:06,740 --> 00:08:08,220
Bills are deducted automatically.

252
00:08:08,220 --> 00:08:09,220
And you have an emergency fund.

253
00:08:09,220 --> 00:08:10,860
And you contribute to retirement from every paycheck.

254
00:08:10,860 --> 00:08:12,340
Breakfast is simple but fresh.

255
00:08:12,340 --> 00:08:13,780
Eggs, toast, fruit.

256
00:08:13,780 --> 00:08:15,060
And if you have kids.

257
00:08:15,060 --> 00:08:17,860
You prep their lunch and check their homework before you leave.

258
00:08:17,860 --> 00:08:18,780
And if you don't.

259
00:08:18,780 --> 00:08:21,180
You make your lunch and save the cost of the cafeteria.

260
00:08:21,180 --> 00:08:22,980
The car is used but clean.

261
00:08:22,980 --> 00:08:25,150
Or you have a reliable train with a monthly pass.

262
00:08:25,150 --> 00:08:26,630
Gas, insurance, and maintenance.

263
00:08:26,630 --> 00:08:27,870
Have become calculated expenses.

264
00:08:27,870 --> 00:08:28,870
Not surprises.

265
00:08:28,870 --> 00:08:30,150
At work, you have a clear role.

266
00:08:30,150 --> 00:08:32,230
With more room to control your day.

267
00:08:32,230 --> 00:08:33,710
Meetings, emails.

268
00:08:33,790 --> 00:08:35,610
Projects that span weeks.

269
00:08:35,610 --> 00:08:38,210
And you have paid time off and you know when to use it.

270
00:08:38,210 --> 00:08:40,450
Insurance and company retirement matching.

271
00:08:40,450 --> 00:08:41,450
Have become the norm.

272
00:08:41,450 --> 00:08:42,810
You dedicate a portion of your income to retirement.

273
00:08:42,810 --> 00:08:44,930
Like 10 to 15%.

274
00:08:44,930 --> 00:08:46,490
And sometimes more if there's a bonus.

275
00:08:46,490 --> 00:08:48,690
And you also have savings for other goals.

276
00:08:48,690 --> 00:08:50,050
At lunch, you open the banking app.

277
00:08:50,050 --> 00:08:51,010
You look at the balance.

278
00:08:51,010 --> 00:08:53,610
Check the monthly installment and transfer a portion to savings.

279
00:08:53,610 --> 00:08:55,850
And if a home repair or new tires are needed.

280
00:08:55,850 --> 00:08:57,810
You have a dedicated fund for it. After work,

281
00:08:57,810 --> 00:08:59,250
You go to the gym, play soccer.

282
00:08:59,250 --> 00:09:01,450
Or go out with friends. You cook most nights.

283
00:09:01,450 --> 00:09:03,410
And order takeout once or twice a week.

284
00:09:03,410 --> 00:09:04,610
Without counting every riyal.

285
00:09:04,610 --> 00:09:05,770
If there's a leak in the house.

286
00:09:05,770 --> 00:09:08,370
You can hire a plumber instead of spending three hours on YouTube.

287
00:09:08,370 --> 00:09:10,650
And you book a dental checkup before it hurts. In the evening,

288
00:09:10,650 --> 00:09:12,370
You help the kids with their homework.

289
00:09:12,370 --> 00:09:13,770
Watch a series or read.

290
00:09:13,770 --> 00:09:15,730
And you can order a birthday gift online.

291
00:09:15,730 --> 00:09:17,450
Without opening the banking app first.

292
00:09:17,450 --> 00:09:19,050
Here, stability is happiness.

293
00:09:19,050 --> 00:09:20,740
The Sixth Class.

294
00:09:20,900 --> 00:09:24,400
The Upper Middle Class.

295
00:09:24,400 --> 00:09:27,280
You wake up in a quiet house you own in an excellent neighborhood.

296
00:09:27,280 --> 00:09:29,100
Or in a very stable home.

297
00:09:29,100 --> 00:09:31,020
The AC adjusted itself at night.

298
00:09:31,020 --> 00:09:33,370
A robot vacuum roams the hallway.

299
00:09:33,370 --> 00:09:35,770
The coffee machine runs on a schedule. You open your phone.

300
00:09:35,770 --> 00:09:37,490
The work calendar, the kids' activities.

301
00:09:37,490 --> 00:09:39,570
A reminder that the cleaner is coming on Friday.

302
00:09:39,570 --> 00:09:41,530
Most bills are paid automatically.

303
00:09:41,530 --> 00:09:43,010
And money is transferred every month to savings.

304
00:09:43,010 --> 00:09:44,930
And investments, without you needing to remember.

305
00:09:44,930 --> 00:09:45,810
Breakfast is varied.

306
00:09:45,810 --> 00:09:46,890
Fresh fruit.

307
00:09:46,890 --> 00:09:48,650
And lunch boxes ready for the kids.

308
00:09:48,650 --> 00:09:50,050
The car is modern and paid off.

309
00:09:50,050 --> 00:09:51,790
Or close to finishing its installments.

310
00:09:51,790 --> 00:09:53,150
Insurance, taxes, and maintenance.

311
00:09:53,150 --> 00:09:54,430
Have become expected costs.

312
00:09:54,430 --> 00:09:55,110
Not crises.

313
00:09:55,110 --> 00:09:57,030
Your job is professional and holds responsibility.

314
00:09:57,030 --> 00:09:57,990
You might manage a team.

315
00:09:57,990 --> 00:09:59,030
You might write code.

316
00:09:59,030 --> 00:09:59,870
Treat patients.

317
00:09:59,870 --> 00:10:01,750
Or handle complex projects.

318
00:10:01,750 --> 00:10:03,310
And you have greater control over your schedule.

319
00:10:03,310 --> 00:10:04,630
Some days you work from home.

320
00:10:04,630 --> 00:10:05,590
And health insurance is strong.

321
00:10:05,590 --> 00:10:06,950
So you do your checkups regularly.

322
00:10:06,950 --> 00:10:08,790
And you don't delay the dentist to the last minute.

323
00:10:08,790 --> 00:10:10,430
And retirement savings run automatically.

324
00:10:10,750 --> 00:10:12,110
And you book a trip months in advance.

325
00:10:12,110 --> 00:10:13,630
And you might use reward points.

326
00:10:13,630 --> 00:10:14,790
To lighten the cost.

327
00:10:14,790 --> 00:10:16,750
If something breaks in the house, you call a professional.

328
00:10:16,750 --> 00:10:18,310
Your time has become more valuable than spending it...

329
00:10:18,310 --> 00:10:20,270
...trying to fix everything yourself.

330
00:10:20,270 --> 00:10:21,750
You pay for landscaping.

331
00:10:21,750 --> 00:10:23,910
And a cleaner visits you regularly. After work,

332
00:10:23,910 --> 00:10:25,820
You might go to the gym with a trainer.

333
00:10:25,820 --> 00:10:27,820
Or take a class. The kids have lessons and sports.

334
00:10:27,820 --> 00:10:29,180
And you can afford the fees and equipment.

335
00:10:29,180 --> 00:10:31,620
At night, you review tomorrow's agenda and sign school papers.

336
00:10:31,620 --> 00:10:33,780
You order a gift online without checking your balance.

337
00:10:33,780 --> 00:10:35,620
And you might donate to a cause you care about.

338
00:10:35,620 --> 00:10:36,980
You feel secure, and most importantly.

339
00:10:36,980 --> 00:10:38,300
You can think about the future.

340
00:10:38,300 --> 00:10:39,980
Without the stress of today weighing you down.

341
00:10:39,980 --> 00:10:41,620
The Seventh Class.

342
00:10:41,620 --> 00:10:44,620
The Wealthy and Comfortable.

343
00:10:44,620 --> 00:10:45,460
Millionaire.

344
00:10:45,460 --> 00:10:48,260
But their life isn't necessarily a show-off.

345
00:10:48,260 --> 00:10:50,340
You wake up in a quiet house you own.

346
00:10:50,340 --> 00:10:51,620
In a highly desired neighborhood.

347
00:10:51,620 --> 00:10:53,940
The mortgage is small, or almost fully paid.

348
00:10:53,940 --> 00:10:55,420
You have a home office.

349
00:10:55,420 --> 00:10:56,660
A guest room.

350
